{
  "dom_id": "step-132146",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents",
  "problem": "Calculate $(-3)^3 \\div 6$.",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we compute the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{(-3)^{3}}_{⏟}}_{-27}÷6=(-27)÷6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-27)÷6 & = \\\\ \\frac{(-27)}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{27}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{27÷3}{6÷3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
